      "content": "The increasing order of boiling points of the following compounds is :\n<img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/jgy2xukfp30kc5/ebdd7bfd-4b83-411c-837d-5caa6d31c7d5/76557250-02f0-11eb-8293-3b6cc591631c/file-jgy2xukfp30kc6-416w.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Main 2020 (Online) 5th September Evening Slot Chemistry - Basics of Organic Chemistry Question 206 English\">",
      "options": [
        {
          "identifier": "A",
          "content": "I &lt; III &lt; IV &lt; II"
        },
        {
          "identifier": "B",
          "content": "IV &lt; I &lt; II &lt; III"
        },
        {
          "identifier": "C",
          "content": "I &lt; IV &lt; III &lt; II"
        },
        {
          "identifier": "D",
          "content": "III &lt; I &lt; II &lt; IV"
        }
      ],
      "correct_options": [
        "C"
      ],
      "explanation": "(I) Shows hydrogen bonding from –OH group only.\n<br><br>(II)  Shows strongest hydrogen bonding from both sides of –OH group as well as –NO<sub>2</sub> group.\n<br><br>(III) Shows stronger hydrogen from both side of –OH group as well as –NH<sub>2</sub> group.\n<br><br>(IV)  Shows stronger hydrogen from one side –OH group and another side of –OCH<sub>3</sub> group shows only\ndipole-dipole interaction.\n<br><br>Hence correct order of boiling point is :\n<br><br>I &lt; IV &lt; III &lt; II"
    }
